REGENT OF KATINGAN

REGENT OF KATINGAN

PROVINCE OF CENTRAL KALIMANTAN

REGIONAL REGULATION OF KATINGAN REGENCY

NUMBER 1 OF 2023

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF KATINGAN,

Considering In View of

: a. that with the enactment of Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 24 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, it is deemed necessary to prevent and address violence against Women and Children through legal protection for Women and Children victims of violence;

b. that based on the consideration as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children victims of violence;

: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the State of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 5 of 2002 concerning the Establishment of Katingan Regency, Seruyan Regency, Sukamara Regency, Lamandau Regency, Gunung Mas Regency, Pulang Pisau Regency, Murung Raya Regency and Barito Timur Regency in Central Kalimantan Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 18, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4180);

3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 100, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);

5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

7. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 13 of 2022 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 143, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6801);

8. Law Number 16 of 2011 concerning Legal Aid (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5246);

9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 238, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6841);

10. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Social Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;

13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;

14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and

Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for

the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service

Centers (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 466);

15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and

Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for

Handling Child Victims of Violence (State News of the

Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 42);

16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and

Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for

Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence (State News of the

Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 903);

17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and

Child Protection Number 2 of 2022 concerning Service

Standards for the Protection of Women and Children (State News of the

Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 85);

With Joint Approval of

THE REGIONAL PEOPLE'S REPRESENTATIVE COUNCIL OF KATINGAN REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF KATINGAN

DECIDES :

To Enact : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

text:
Pasal 2

Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan, dilaksanakan berdasarkan asas :

a. penghormatan dan pemenuhan terhadap hak-hak korban;
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. non diskriminasi;
d. kepentingan terbaik bagi korban;
e. kearifan lokal;
f. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup dan perkembangan anak; g. penghargaan terhadap pendapat korban; dan
h. kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
Article 2

Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence is implemented based on the principles of:

a. respect and fulfillment of victims' rights;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. best interests of victims;
e. local wisdom;
f. right to life, survival and development of children; g. respect for victims' opinions; and
h. legal certainty.

text:
Pasal 4

Ruang lingkup Pengaturan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan meliputi:

a. hak korban;
b. kewenangan, kewajiban dan tanggung jawab;
c. kelembagaan;
d. standar pelayanan minimal;
e. rumah perlindungan sosial;
f. pelaporan;
g. pembinaan dan pengawasan;
h. peran serta masyarakat; dan
i. pendanaan.

translated_text:
Article 4

The Scope of Regulation of Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence includes:

a. victims' rights;
b. authority, obligations and responsibilities;
c. institutions;
d. minimum service standards;
e. social protection house;
f. reporting;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. community participation; and
i. funding.

text:
Pasal 5

Setiap Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan berhak :

a. untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia;
b. untuk mendapatkan perlindungan dari keluarga, masyarakat, Pemerintah Daerah dan pihak lain baik sementara maupun berdasarkan penetapan perintah Perlindungan dari Pengadilan;
c. mendapatkan pemulihan pelayanan kesehatan fisik, psikologis maupun seksual sesuai penderitaan yang dialami oleh korban kekerasan;
d. mendapatkan penanganan secara khusus berkaitan dengan kerahasiaan korban; e. mendapatkan pendampingan oleh pendamping dan bantuan hukum pada setiap tingkat proses pemeriksaan sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan;
f. mendapatkan pelayanan bimbingan rohani.

translated_text:
Article 5

Every Woman and Child victim of violence has the right:

a. to have their dignity respected as human beings;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and other parties either temporarily or based on a Protection Order from the Court;
c. to obtain recovery health services physically, psychologically or sexually according to the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
d. to obtain special handling related to victim confidentiality; e. to obtain assistance by companions and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to obtain spiritual guidance services.

text:
Pasal 7

(1) Pemerintah Daerah berwenang dan bertanggung jawab atas Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan.

(2) Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. menjamin hak perempuan dan anak tanpa diskriminasi sesuai peraturan perundang-undangan;
b. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan berdasarkan peraturan perundang-undangan;
c. menetapkan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan;
d. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan;
e. mengalokasikan anggaran dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan;
f. membina dan mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan;
g. peningkatan kualitas dan kompetensi SDM yang memberikan pelayanan/ pendampingan bagi korban kekerasan pada perempuan dan anak; h. melakukan keijasama dengan masyarakat dan/atau organisasi kemasyarakatan dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan sesuai dengan peraturan perundang-undangan;
i. melakukan tindakan preventive dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya pelanggaran terhadap hak perempuan dan anak.
(3) Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya perlindungan perempuan dan anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada Pasal 7 ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh Perangkat Daerah sesuai dengan tugas dan fungsinya.

translated_text:
Article 7

(1) The Regional Government has the authority and responsibility for the Protection of Women and Children who are victims of violence.

(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. guaranteeing the rights of women and children without discrimination in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. implementing policies for the protection of Women and Children who are victims of violence based on laws and regulations;
c. establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women and Children who are victims of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of Women and Children who are victims of violence;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of Women and Children who are victims of violence;
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of Women and Children who are victims of violence;
g. improving the quality and competence of human resources who provide services/assistance for victims of violence against women and children; h. conducting cooperation with the community and/or community organizations in the implementation of protection of women in accordance with laws and regulations;
i. carrying out preventive actions in order to prevent violations of the rights of women and children.
(3) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to protect women and children as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (1) is carried out by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

text:
Pasal 9

(1) UPTD PPA yang telah terbentuk dapat mewadahi lembaga/unit keija yang memberikan pelayanan bagi korban kekerasan seperti rumah aman, rumah perlindungan sosial Anak, rumah perlindungan trauma center, rumah perlindungan sosial wanita, rumah singgah dan lain-lain kegiatan pelayanan sesuai Peraturan Perundang-undangan yang berlaku.

(2) Bentuk pelayanan yang dilaksanakan UPTD PPA meliputi :

a. penanganan pengaduan;
b. rehabilitasi kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. bantuan hukum;
e. pemulihan/layanan psikologis;
f. mediasi; dan
g. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
(3) Pemberian layanan terpadu sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dilaksanakan sesuai dengan SPM.

translated_text:
Article 9

(1) The UPTD PPA that has been established may accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as safe houses, children's social protection houses, trauma center protection houses, women's social protection houses, shelters and other service activities in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.

(2) The forms of services implemented by UPTD PPA include:

a. handling complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal assistance;
e. recovery/psychological services;
f. mediation; and
g. repatriation and social reintegration.
(3) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (2) is implemented in accordance with SPM.

text:
Pasal 11

(1) SPM sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 ayat (3) memiliki indikator kineija meliputi :

a. cakupan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan yang mendapatkan penanganan pengaduan oleh petugas terlatih di dalam UPTD PPA; b. cakupan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan yang mendapatkan layanan kesehatan oleh tenaga kesehatan terlatih di Puskesmas dan di Rumah Sakit;
c. cakupan layanan rehabilitasi sosial yang diberikan oleh petugas rehabilitasi sosial terlatih bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan di dalam UPTD PPA;
d. cakupan layanan bimbingan rohani yang diberikan oleh petugas bimbingan rohani terlatih bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan di dalam UPTD PPA;
e. cakupan layanan bantuan hukum bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
f. cakupan layanan pemulihan/ layanan psikologis bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
g. cakupan layanan mediasi bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; h. cakupan layanan pemulangan bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; dan
i. cakupan layanan reintegrasi sosial bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.
(2) Penetapan indikator kineija SPM UPTD PPA bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan target minimal yang harus dicapai.

translated_text:
Article 11

(1) SPM as referred to in Article 9 paragraph (3) has performance indicators including:

a. coverage of Women and Children who are victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers within UPTD PPA; b. coverage of Women and Children who are victims of violence who receive health services by trained health personnel at Puskesmas and Hospitals;
c. coverage of social rehabilitation services provided by trained social rehabilitation officers for Women and Children who are victims of violence within UPTD PPA;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women and Children who are victims of violence within UPTD PPA;
e. coverage of legal assistance services for women and children who are victims of violence;
f. coverage of recovery/psychological services for women and children who are victims of violence;
g. coverage of mediation services for women and children who are victims of violence; h. coverage of repatriation services for women and children who are victims of violence; and
i. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children who are victims of violence.
(2) The determination of performance indicators of SPM UPTD PPA for Women and Children who are victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) constitutes the minimum target that must be achieved.

text:
Pasal 14

(1) Bupati melakukan pembinaan dan pengawasan penyelenggaraan UPTD PPA. (2) Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. pedoman dan standar pemenuhan;
b. bimbingan teknis dan pelatihan;
c. supervisi;
d. penyediaan fasilitas;
e. monitoring; dan
f. evaluasi.
(3) Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dalam rangka mewujudkan tujuan perlindungan perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sesuai standar pelayanan minimal.

translated_text:
Article 14

(1) The Regent conducts development and supervision of the implementation of UPTD PPA. (2) Development as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:

a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. supervision;
d. provision of facilities;
e. monitoring; and
f. evaluation.
(3) Development as referred to in paragraph (2) is in order to realize the objectives of protection of women and Children who are victims of violence in accordance with minimum service standards.
